# Allowlist for scripts/check-stale-candidate-refs.sh.
#
# The current candidate is v0.10.0-rc.10. References to the superseded
# v0.10.0-rc.8 and v0.10.0-rc.9 candidates (pattern: rc\.8|20cc13a|rc\.9|07d2ba2)
# are allowed only in the historical records below. Rule syntax is documented
# in the script header.

# Historical identity record for rc.8 (later candidates are recorded on their
# certification branches).
file docs/releases/v0.10-candidate-identity-reconciliation.md
# Per-candidate release notes are point-in-time records.
file docs/releases/v0.10.0-rc.*.md
# Archived notes are historical by definition (AGENTS.md).
file docs/archive/*

# VERSION_HISTORY history sections.
section docs/releases/VERSION_HISTORY.md ### v0.10.0-rc.8 — Divergent stabilization candidate (superseded)
section docs/releases/VERSION_HISTORY.md ### v0.10.0-rc.9 — Worker idempotency and attribution fixes (superseded)

# Certification record: rc.9 and rc.8 identities kept as history below the
# rc.10 record.
section docs/releases/v0.10-core-staging-certification.md ## Historical rc.9 candidate identity (superseded)
section docs/releases/v0.10-core-staging-certification.md ## Historical rc.8 candidate identity (superseded)

# Lines that explicitly label the reference as superseded or historical.
line superseded|historical

# The approval finalization defect range (rc.1 through rc.9), as written in the
# remediation runbook and the rc.10 notes: "rc.1 through rc.9", "rc.1-rc.9",
# "rc.1–rc.9", "`v0.10.0-rc.1` through `v0.10.0-rc.9`".
line rc\.1`?( through | to |-|–)`?(v0\.10\.0-)?rc\.9

# Behaviour attributed to the rc.9 change set, which later candidates keep
# ("since rc.9", "before rc.9", "fixed in rc.9", "resolved in `v0.10.0-rc.9`").
line (since|before|fixed in|resolved in|changed in) `?(v0\.10\.0-)?rc\.9
